| D-011 | 2026-10-27 | all orgs     | CI provider is GitHub Actions (default), CircleCI, or both, chosen with hull pieces `circleci`/`circleci-only`; required check names never change (CircleCI's ci-ok is mirrored to a commit status); governance, PR previews, splice bot and releases stay on GitHub Actions; D-007 rules apply to CircleCI. [why](decisions/011-ci-providers.md)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                |
{% if "portable" in pieces %}{% else %}| D-012 | 2026-10-29 | all          | Owner approvals are asked as a Claude Code chat form naming repo, PR and head SHA; the orchestrator posts the signed bosun approval (owner GitHub comments still count, never requested). Bootstrap mode until 2026-11-30 UTC: the orchestrator may approve gated PRs itself after green checks and an independent review of that head; environments, tags, releases, decisions merges, branch rules and secrets still need the owner. [why](decisions/012-approvals-by-form-and-bootstrap-mode.md)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |
{% endif %}{% if "portable" in pieces %}{% else %}| D-013 | 2026-10-29 | all          | During bootstrap mode (D-012, until 2026-11-30): low-risk PRs (docs, site, tests, new self-contained code, one package with no gated path) may reach 1,500 changed lines and bundle related tasks; gated PRs (workflows, templates, contract, governance, .bosun, approval code, secrets, environments, releases) stay at most 400 lines and one task. Tests, lockfiles and generated files do not count. [why](decisions/013-bootstrap-pr-size.md)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              |
{% endif %}{% if "portable" in pieces %}{% else %}| D-014 | 2026-11-03 | all          | Approval policy after bootstrap mode is the intake answer `[approvals] policy` in `.bosun/intake.toml`: `owner` (default when unset), `owner-gated` (orchestrator approves low-risk and R-ci after green checks and an independent review; owner approves R-gov, `.bosun`, approval code, workflows, secrets, releases) or `orchestrator`. In every policy the owner approves environment deployments, decisions merges, branch rules and secrets, and CI-workflow or composite-action PRs are owner-class. Repos are created and configured only by the org provisioner app via keelstackhq/provision, gated by a one-hour, single-use orchestrator signature made on an owner form answer; secrets are environment-only; no PAT. [why](decisions/014-zero-touch-onboarding.md) |
{% endif %}{% if "portable" in pieces %}{% else %}| D-015 | 2026-11-02 | all          | Child sessions never merge PRs, push or move tags, start releases, or force-push; they get required checks green (`ci-ok`; bosun also risk-check, review-verdict, main-open), may enable `gh pr merge --auto`. The orchestrator may merge once required checks are green and any owner approval is in, and may start a release via the repo's release workflow (`workflow_dispatch` or the version-bump merge) after green CI and an independent review; the workflow creates the tag; the owner approves `release`; decisions stays owner-merged. [why](decisions/015-orchestrator-starts-releases.md)                                                                                                                                                                          |
